const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文以概率模型连接财务比率、企业规模等会计信息与困境结果。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源将多个报告变量放进概率预测框架，并围绕明确的困境标签和样本定义讨论结果。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"必须保留财务比率的原始分子分母、公司规模、困境定义、财年、披露时间和证券映射。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"模型说明会计变量可被用于研究困境结果的条件关联，但不把估计概率视为某家公司必然的未来状态。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"以披露时点而非财年末对齐输入，记录重述、合并范围和标签期限，并检查类别不平衡与样本外定义。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Accounting Research (1980)。破产制度、会计准则和公司样本随时间与国家变化；历史概率模型不构成当前信用判断或融资建议。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Accounting Research (1980) for “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2490395",label:{zh:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Accounting Research (1980) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。破产制度、会计准则和公司样本随时间与国家变化；历史概率模型不构成当前信用判断或融资建议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Financial Ratios and the Probabilistic Prediction of Bankruptcy”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
